{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChFL8tVdXx3Ay8KfdQvpE","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[x] `setup()` given an adversarial config writes `.redeye.json` with `implement`, `review`, `maxRounds` and `minRounds`\n[x] `setup()` given an adversarial config and an existing `.redeye.json` with other keys keeps those keys and adds `adversarial`\n[x] `setup()` with no adversarial config leaves an existing `.redeye.json` untouched and creates none when it is absent\n\nTicket 03 is done. Earlier commits on this branch (US-007 and its follow-ups) had already built most of it, so I only had to check it and fix one spot.\n\n**Already there:** `setup()` writes and merges the `adversarial` key in `src/setup.ts`. `test/setup.test.ts` already had a test for each of the three checklist items, and they pass. The `init` prompts were also there, but the adversarial question came after the \"this skill already exists, overwrite?\" prompts instead of right after the tracker question.\n\n**What I changed (commit `46cd48f`):**\n1. In `src/index.ts`, the adversarial question now comes right after the tracker question, as the spec says. It now reads \"Run an adversarial review loop on each ticket?\" and still defaults to no. I merged the two identical validation blocks into one `validateRoleString`. An invalid command string shows the error and asks again.\n2. In `README.md`, the `init` paragraph now covers the default of no, asking again on an invalid string, the `maxRounds: 3` / `minRounds: 1` defaults, keeping other keys in an existing file, and leaving the file alone on no.\n\nI added no tests: the ticket says the prompts stay untested, and the `setup()` tests already existed. Lint, build and the full `npm test` run all pass.\n\n**Not fixed (outside this ticket):** if an existing `.redeye.json` is not valid JSON, `setup()` fails only at the very end, after the skills and docs are already installed. The run exits 2 wi